course: dictionary
lesson: 10183
title: Tigress: a female tiger, and a fierce woman
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tigress is a female tiger. The -ess ending often marks a female, as in lioness. Read the words around a new word to find clues. In «Tigress and Crane are fighters in the film, and their real animals are just as amazing: a tiger that loves a swim and a bird that dances in the snow», the words real animals and a tiger tell you that a tigress is an animal too.
explain: A tigress can also describe a person. When a woman is fierce and brave, especially when she protects her children, we can call her a tigress. «She fought like a tigress» shows that she was fierce and would not give up. This is a figurative meaning: the word is used to describe a feeling or a quality, not a real animal.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «She fought like a fierce, brave woman» still make sense? Yes, so your meaning fits. If you read «She fought like a tiny cat», the sentence does not make sense, so that meaning is wrong.
fact: A tigress is a female tiger.
fact: A tigress can also mean a woman who is fierce and brave, especially when protecting her children.
fact: «She fought like a tigress» shows fierce courage.
fact: A tigress raises her cubs alone for about two years and teaches them to hunt.
fact: Tigers are endangered, and they live in parts of Asia.
exercise: «Tigress and Crane are fighters in the film, and their real animals are just as amazing: a tiger that loves a swim and a bird that dances in the snow.» What is a tigress? | A bird that dances in the snow | A fighter in a film | A tiger that loves a swim | *A female tiger
exercise: «She fought like a tigress to protect her cubs.» What does tigress mean here? | A tiny cat | A bird that dances | *A fierce, brave woman | A slow, sleepy animal
exercise: A tigress raises her cubs alone for about two years. Who looks after the cubs? | *The tigress | Nobody | The tiger father | The hunters
test: «Tigers are endangered; they live in parts of Asia.» Where do tigers live? | In parts of Europe only | *In parts of Asia | In the sea | In the snow of the Arctic
test: What does -ess tell you in tigress? | That the animal is very big | That the animal is in danger | That the animal is a bird | *That the animal is female
exam: «She fought like a tigress.» What does the sentence show about her? | She was weak and frightened | She was lost in the snow | She was sleepy and tired | *She was fierce and brave
